<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flammŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little flame.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Timagoras negat sibi umquam, cum oculum
					torsisset, duas ex lucerna flammulas esse visas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 25, 80</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 14, 9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in late Lat., <i>a
				little banner</i> used by cavalry, <i><span class="en">Veg.
				Mil. 2, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
